<description>External Audio</description>
<plain>
<wire x1="193.04" y1="254" x2="378.46" y2="254" width="0.1524" layer="94"/>
<wire x1="378.46" y1="254" x2="378.46" y2="127" width="0.1524" layer="94"/>
<wire x1="378.46" y1="127" x2="193.04" y2="127" width="0.1524" layer="94"/>
<wire x1="193.04" y1="127" x2="193.04" y2="254" width="0.1524" layer="94"/>
<text x="195.58" y="246.38" size="3.81" layer="94">External Codec</text>
<text x="307.34" y="233.68" size="1.778" layer="91">MODE Pin:
VDD - SPI Mode
VDD via 220K pullup - H/W Mode, single-ended VoutX.
GND via 220K pulldown - H/W Mode, differential VoutX.
GND - I2C Mode</text>
<text x="241.3" y="213.36" size="1.778" layer="91">220K pulldown for differential SAI</text>
<text x="269.24" y="134.62" size="1.778" layer="91">for full hardware compatibility with Seed1:
R23 should be DNI
R4 should be populated (4K7 is fine)

This will hard code:
* FMT to 24 Bit LJ (via R22)
* DEMPhasis filter OFF

Otherwise PB11 will need to be pulled low in software
to compensate for the pullup that sets the deemphasis filter to 44.1kHz</text>
<wire x1="10.16" y1="58.42" x2="10.16" y2="254" width="0.1524" layer="94"/>
<wire x1="10.16" y1="254" x2="187.96" y2="254" width="0.1524" layer="94"/>
<wire x1="187.96" y1="254" x2="187.96" y2="58.42" width="0.1524" layer="94"/>
<wire x1="187.96" y1="58.42" x2="10.16" y2="58.42" width="0.1524" layer="94"/>
<text x="12.7" y="246.38" size="3.81" layer="94">External Codec Audio I/O</text>
<text x="195.58" y="119.38" size="3.81" layer="94">Using S2DFM codec_vcom instead...</text>
</plain>
